---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { PRIVACY_PATH, REFUNDS_PATH, SITE_BRAND, TERMS_PATH } from '../../lib/seo';
---

<LegalLayout
	title="Content License"
	description="iStockVisual.com license: commercial and personal use of library images, attribution required, all sizes and formats."
	heading="Content License"
	lede="Library images are licensed for commercial and personal use. Attribution is required on every size — including 512, 1K, and Pro downloads."
>
	<h2>1. What this license covers</h2>
	<p>
		This license applies to photos, illustrations, vectors, and 3D stills published in the
		{SITE_BRAND} library (“Library Content”), including files you download from a detail page and
		recognizable derivatives you make with the on-page editor or the studio tools. Most Library
		Content is generated or prepared for this site. It is not public domain. Downloading a file does
		not transfer copyright to you.
	</p>
	<p>
		<strong>512</strong> and <strong>1K</strong> (1024 long edge) are free. <strong>2K</strong>,
		<strong>4K</strong>, and <strong>8K</strong> need an active Pro plan or pass. The same license
		applies to every size and to JPG, PNG, WEBP, and SVG. A larger file does not buy a broader
		license — only more pixels.
	</p>

	<h2>2. What you may do</h2>
	<p>Subject to this license and our <a href={TERMS_PATH}>Terms of Use</a>, you may:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			Use Library Content in personal and commercial projects: websites, ads, social posts, decks,
			packaging, editorial layouts, and print
		</li>
		<li>
			Edit, crop, color-grade, remove background, expand, convert format, vectorize, resize for
			social frames, watermark, or composite with your own work
		</li>
		<li>Use Library Content in client work, provided the client also follows this license</li>
		<li>Keep files you already downloaded if a plan later ends, still subject to this license</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>3. Attribution</h2>
	<p>
		You must credit the source whenever Library Content is used in a context where a credit can
		reasonably appear (websites, videos, print, apps, and similar). Use wording equivalent to:
	</p>
	<p><strong>Generated by {SITE_BRAND}</strong></p>
	<p>
		A link to the image’s public page (or to {SITE_BRAND}) is preferred when the medium allows it.
		Each asset page includes copy-ready credit. Do not strip a required credit from an unmodified
		library file you pass along as part of a larger work.
	</p>
	<p>
		If a layout has no room for a visible credit (for example a small app icon), put the same
		wording in an about, credits, or description field that users can open.
	</p>

	<h2>4. What you may not do</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			Sell, license, or redistribute the original or lightly modified file as a standalone stock
			asset, prompt pack, or competing library item
		</li>
		<li>Claim exclusive ownership of unmodified Library Content, or register it as your trademark or copyright</li>
		<li>Use Library Content to imply that iStockVisual endorses a person, product, or cause</li>
		<li>Use Library Content in unlawful, deceptive, or hateful material</li>
		<li>
			Scrape, bulk-harvest, or automate downloads beyond ordinary personal or studio use, including
			after the HD fair-use cap in the Terms
		</li>
		<li>Share Pro login details so others can download HD files on your account</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>5. Browser tools and your own files</h2>
	<p>
		Image Editor, Convert, Vectorizer, Social Resizer, Batch Watermark, and Palette Generator run in
		your browser. Files you choose on your device for those tools are not uploaded to iStockVisual
		and remain yours. If you start from Library Content, this license and the attribution
		requirement still apply to that content and to recognizable derivatives of it.
	</p>
	<p>
		On-page editor exports from library files follow the same size rules as downloads: free users
		stay on 512 / 1K; Pro may export larger tiers. Expand on library assets is a Pro feature.
	</p>
	<p>
		Visual search may upload a query photo so we can match the library. That upload is handled under
		the <a href={PRIVACY_PATH}>Privacy Policy</a> and is not added to the public library.
	</p>

	<h2>6. Trademarks, people, and generated scenes</h2>
	<p>
		Library Content is produced for general creative use. Scenes may be generated or stylized. You
		are responsible for extra clearance your project needs — for example real trademarks, logos, or
		identifiable people that you add, or regulated claims you make next to an image. Do not treat a
		generated interior, product, or skyline as a photo of a specific real property or brand unless
		you have independently verified that.
	</p>

	<h2>7. Fair use, refunds, and changes</h2>
	<p>
		HD speed limits do not change this license. Refunds are in the
		<a href={REFUNDS_PATH}>Refund Policy</a>. We may update this license; the version on this page
		applies to new downloads from the date it is posted. Files you already downloaded remain usable
		under the license that applied when you downloaded them, unless we must restrict use to comply
		with law.
	</p>
</LegalLayout>
